  "goodToKnow": "Das Elfenbein is ivory. Despite appearances, it has nothing to do with elves: it comes from an old word for elephant (elfent) and Bein, which once meant bone. The international ivory trade was banned in 1989 under CITES to protect elephants. Im Elfenbeinturm sitzen means to live in an ivory tower, and die Elfenbeinküste is Ivory Coast. The oldest known figurative art, carved from mammoth ivory, was found in caves of the Swabian Jura."
